    "created_at": "2026-01-30T06:34:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-30T06:34:08Z",
    "body": "A member of a dictionary being nullable is sometimes needed, because people expect to be able to pass in an object of the same shape for instance, which has getters that return null. I don't think it's needed in the FS case though.\n\nPerhaps we should require an attribute for the \"object-of-the-same-shape\" type though and try to outlaw it in the normal case.",
